<description>&lt;p&gt;Government forces and opposition fighters clashed, leaving 23 dead and prompting governors in Jonglei and Aweil East to call for peace and justice. A Ugandan truck driver and a companion were killed in an ambush and their bodies were released by South Sudanese authorities. The Mayom County commissioner and his family were assassinated, while a soldier and a civilian were killed in an attack in Kapoeta North. Communal fighting in Tonj East resulted in 11 deaths before calm returned, and churches reported worship disruptions due to violence. Two battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Hindu&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinAFBVV95cUxOV1BiSGxhaFB2VVlla3VUSzI1WFBuaGlaWHZJaWo1QzZDRjdZd05IMktabVZ6RGtGY2FTSFBjbEhJbnRlcXp5enNaTnlya3RkZlJPWHBHQ2ZzcU5tVlVMbEF0UmI5RFpKODVoRlNlVWc2MXdCSTVyblAyalRtTlN3UjBmY0tzQUJDU3p3VG1WcTdkQlFqbHZJVHppa3g?oc=5&quot;&gt;Christian Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMid0FVX3lxTE5ScDR4ODFLdHBhU3ZPVFdPRHZSOGZ4Nmo1WnhXQ0lXVUxGZGFTLUYwS0JMTmtpQ1diMGw1b2ctRFRMeTVKcC1NbjhKZ3lCY0t2QUNnYVRlVnY1Uy1PcXhrZjBOdVdwdnJXdFU0aDZvU09xbkRrazdN?oc=5&quot;&gt;Times of Suriname&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiaEFVX3lxTE43ZGR3Wno1WHpjU2ExOFpXTHlRZVZpU2Y1eHhEdGlNSkhpQm9GYXFRUjJ0V1lkWThHUjFpSks0MFhHMFNQM3FUU3Y4OTNVOERuUWJEbnhDNlNoelhwS1BBVklGNC1NVElH?oc=5&quot;&gt;Uganda Radionetwork&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiZEFVX3lxTE9XYXRtdUVzUzllcEI2TDVVUmd4clM0SEEtNlBtOXNKSWhUWUdWUk9tUVlSQmNralRkR2ZoSW1GeW9rV0VTTGJvYkcxZE5LQWpQN2ZDOG43ZE9KX0VsampOcXZVX2Y?oc=5&quot;&gt;Daily Trust&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.